IMPORT prelude
IMPORT `cbca-core`
IMPORT `cbca-core-definitions`

-- Canada Business Corporations Act (R.S.C. 1985, c. C-44), piece cb4 (Parts XV to XVIII) -- SHARED NOUNS
-- AND HELPERS.
--
-- UNOFFICIAL. The text this was encoded from is a plain-text rendering of the Department of Justice
-- Canada consolidation current to 2026-09-30 (last amended 2026-03-26); it is not an official version,
-- and nothing here has been verified against the official text.
--
-- WHAT THIS MODULE IS. The few types and helper rules that two or more cb4 modules (or the seat layer)
-- use. A helper encodes no provision of its own; it computes something the provisions share, and it is
-- named for what it computes, with no section suffix. Every other type is declared in the module that
-- needs it and carries the section in its name. Every top-level name in the cb4 modules is unique
-- across the Act, because the seat layer imports them all and a name defined in two imported modules
-- cannot be used at all.
--
-- CONVENTIONS: as in the keel (cbca-core.l4). Days are a NUMBER; a time limit in other units is a
-- `Time limit`; a fraction is a NUMBER from 0 to 1 written with %; a case the text does not answer is a
-- named constructor or NOTHING, never FALSE or 0.

§ `Shared helpers for Parts XV to XVIII`

§§ `Resolutions of several classes`

-- Several sections ask for a special (or ordinary) resolution of the holders of EACH class or series
-- entitled to vote separately (ss 176(6), 183(5), 189(8), 194, 210(2) and (3), 211(3)). Each class's
-- votes are one `Vote tally`; the classes together are a list. The helpers are rules about the keel's
-- own definitions, so they restate nothing: they apply `special resolution within s 2(1)` and
-- `ordinary resolution within s 2(1)` to every tally. A list with no tally in it is "every class"
-- vacuously: no class had to vote.
-- src:72 | special resolution means a resolution passed by a majority of not less than two-thirds of the votes cast by the shareholders who voted in respect of that resolution or signed by all the shareholders entitled to vote on that resolution; (résolution spéciale)
@ref CBCA s 2(1) special resolution, helper (src:72)
GIVEN tallies IS A LIST OF `Vote tally`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`every tally in the list passes as a special resolution` tallies MEANS
    all (GIVEN t YIELD `special resolution within s 2(1)` t) tallies

-- src:55 | ordinary resolution means a resolution passed by a majority of the votes cast by the shareholders who voted in respect of that resolution; (résolution ordinaire)
@ref CBCA s 2(1) ordinary resolution, helper (src:55)
GIVEN tallies IS A LIST OF `Vote tally`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`every tally in the list passes as an ordinary resolution` tallies MEANS
    all (GIVEN t YIELD `ordinary resolution within s 2(1)` t) tallies

§§ `Dates`

-- "The later of two days" (s 190(12), s 206.1(1)(b)) and "the day before" (s 190(3)).
-- src:2396 | (12) A corporation shall, not later than seven days after the later of the day on which the action approved by the resolution is effective or the day the corporation received the notice referred to in subsection (7), send to each dissenting shareholder who has sent such notice
-- src:2572 | (b) if the shareholder did not receive an offer pursuant to the take-over bid, within ninety days after the later of
@ref CBCA s 190(12), s 206.1(1)(b), helper (src:2396 src:2572)
GIVEN first IS A DATE
      second IS A DATE
GIVETH A DATE
`the later of two dates` first second MEANS
    IF first AT LEAST second THEN first ELSE second

-- "Within sixty days after termination, and in any event within one hundred and eighty days after the
-- bid": the notice must satisfy both limits, so its last day is the EARLIER of the two last days.
-- src:2511 | (3) An offeror may acquire shares held by a dissenting offeree by sending by registered mail within sixty days after the date of termination of the take-over bid and in any event within one hundred and eighty days after the date of the take-over bid, an offeror’s notice to each dissenting offeree and to the Director stating that
@ref CBCA s 206(3), helper (src:2511)
GIVEN first IS A DATE
      second IS A DATE
GIVETH A DATE
`the earlier of two dates` first second MEANS
    IF first AT MOST second THEN first ELSE second

-- src:2371 | (3) In addition to any other right the shareholder may have, but subject to subsection (26), a shareholder who complies with this section is entitled, when the action approved by the resolution from which the shareholder dissents or an order made under subsection 192(4) becomes effective, to be paid by the corporation the fair value of the shares in respect of which the shareholder dissents, determined as of the close of business on the day before the resolution was adopted or the order was made.
@ref CBCA s 190(3), helper (src:2371)
GIVEN day IS A DATE
GIVETH A DATE
`the day immediately before` day MEANS
    day MINUS 1

§§ `Leaving out the statement of the right to dissent`

-- Four sections require a notice of a meeting to state that a dissenting shareholder is entitled to be
-- paid the fair value of their shares, and say that failure to make the statement does not invalidate
-- the action (ss 175(2), 183(2)(b), 188(3), 189(4)(b)). The Act says nothing about the effect of any
-- OTHER failure of the notice, so that case is a named answer, never "invalid" and never "valid".
-- src:2151 | (2) Notice of a meeting of shareholders at which a proposal to amend the articles is to be considered shall set out the proposed amendment and, where applicable, shall state that a dissenting shareholder is entitled to be paid the fair value of their shares in accordance with section 190, but failure to make that statement does not invalidate an amendment.
-- src:2212 | (b) state that a dissenting shareholder is entitled to be paid the fair value of their shares in accordance with section 190, but failure to make that statement does not invalidate an amalgamation.
-- src:2314 | (3) A notice of a meeting of shareholders complying with section 135 shall be sent in accordance with that section to each shareholder and shall state that a dissenting shareholder is entitled to be paid the fair value of their shares in accordance with section 190, but failure to make that statement does not invalidate a discontinuance under this Act.
-- src:2347 | (b) state that a dissenting shareholder is entitled to be paid the fair value of their shares in accordance with section 190, but failure to make that statement does not invalidate a sale, lease or exchange referred to in subsection (3).
@ref CBCA s 175(2), s 183(2)(b), s 188(3), s 189(4)(b), helper (src:2151 src:2212 src:2314 src:2347)
DECLARE `Effect on validity of leaving out the dissent statement` IS ONE OF
    `the omission does not make the action invalid`
    `the Act does not say whether the omission makes the action invalid`

GIVEN `the omission of the dissent statement was the only failure of the notice` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A `Effect on validity of leaving out the dissent statement`
`the effect of leaving out the dissent statement` MEANS
    IF `the omission of the dissent statement was the only failure of the notice`
    THEN `the omission does not make the action invalid`
    ELSE `the Act does not say whether the omission makes the action invalid`

§§ `Whether a provision protects a matter`

-- Several sections say that something "does not affect" or "is unaffected": existing causes of action
-- and the like. For a matter inside the listed class the answer is TRUE; for a matter outside it the
-- section is silent, which is NOTHING, not FALSE.
-- src:2185 | (2) No amendment to the articles affects an existing cause of action or claim or liability to prosecution in favour of or against the corporation or its directors or officers, or any civil, criminal or administrative action or proceeding to which a corporation or its directors or officers is a party.
-- src:2258 | (d) an existing cause of action, claim or liability to prosecution is unaffected;
@ref CBCA s 179(2), s 186(d), helper (src:2185 src:2258)
GIVEN `the matter is one the provision lists` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`whether a listed matter is unaffected` MEANS
    IF `the matter is one the provision lists` THEN JUST TRUE ELSE NOTHING
